  "issue_number": 12032,
  "issue_title": "angular-query: migrate-from-experimental schematic crashes with 'Path ... is a file' on a .js subpath import",
  "issue_body": "### Describe the bug\n\nThe `migrate-from-experimental` schematic in `@tanstack/angular-query@5.0.0-rc.3` aborts before migrating anything when a project source imports a package subpath that names a file, such as `import { sha3_256 } from '@noble/hashes/sha3.js'`:\n\n```\nPath \"/node_modules/@noble/hashes/sha3.js\" is a file.\n```\n\nThe cause is the compiler host built in `configuredSources()` (`packages/angular-query/schematics/migrate-from-experimental/workspace.ts`). Its `directoryExists` calls `tree.getDir(path)` directly. TypeScript's module resolution probes candidate paths with `directoryExists`, and some of them are files. The devkit `Tree.getDir()` then throws `PathIsFileException` rather than reporting that no directory exists.\n\n### Your minimal, reproducible example\n\nhttps://github.com/imaksp/tanstack-angular-query-migrate-schematic-repro\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Clone the repro and run `pnpm install`.\n2. Run `pnpm exec ng generate @tanstack/angular-query:migrate-from-experimental --dry-run`.\n3. See `Path \"/node_modules/@noble/hashes/sha3.js\" is a file.`\n\nIt also reproduces with an npm-style flat layout (`pnpm install --config.node-linker=hoisted`). Removing the `@noble/hashes/sha3.js` import makes the dry run succeed.\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nThe schematic migrates the workspace: the dry run lists `UPDATE src/main.ts` and `UPDATE package.json`. Instead it throws, and none of the project's files are migrated. In a real workspace, every file is skipped as soon as one source imports such a subpath.\n\n### How often does this bug happen?\n\nEvery time\n\n### Platform\n\n- OS: macOS 26\n- Node: 26.8.2\n- pnpm: 12.9.1\n- Angular CLI: 22.2.1\n\n### Tanstack Query adapter\n\nangular-query\n\n### TanStack Query version\n\n5.0.0-rc.3\n\n### TypeScript version\n\n6.0.3\n\n### Additional context\n\nMaking `directoryExists` return `false` for a path that is a file fixes it. `tree.exists()` is true only for files:\n\n```ts\nhost.directoryExists = (path) => {\n  if (tree.exists(path)) return false\n  const directory = tree.getDir(path)\n  return directory.subfiles.length > 0 || directory.subdirs.length > 0\n}\n```\n\nWith that change the repro's dry run succeeds. I'll open a PR with the fix and a regression test.\n",
  "merged_at": "2026-10-16T11:49:25Z",
